<title>USA: Sequa to appeal denial of injunction.</title>
<headline>Sequa to appeal denial of injunction.</headline>
<dateline>SAN ANTONIO 1997-04-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sequa Corp's Chromalloy Gas Turbine Corp said Thursday it will appeal a Texas court's decision not to bar United Technologies Corp's Pratt &amp; Whitney from &quot;its monopolistic conduct.&quot;</p>
<p>In November a Texas jury decided Pratt &amp; Whitney had violated state antitrust laws by trying to monopolize the replacement business for its jet engine parts, Chromalloy said. The company said it sought the injunction based on that verdict.</p>
<p>Chromalloy said it wants the court to lay down guidelines to prevent Pratt from trying to restrain competition in the area of repair and replacement parts.</p>
</text>
